hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20799","Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, and Ibn Bakr informed us, Ibn Jurayj, and Abu Asim, from Ibn Jurayj, Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Said informed me, that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him, that al-Saib ibn Yazid informed him, that he heard al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajir remains in Makkah after completing his rites for three. Abu Asim said: Three nights."
"20800","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, he said: I heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz asking al-Saib: What did you hear about residing in Makkah? So he said: Al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami told me that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the Muhajir, three after the Sadar."
"20801","Abdullah narrated to us, my father and Yahya ibn Ma'in told me, both said: Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mughirah al-Azdi from Muhammad ibn Zayd from Hayyan al-A'raj from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Bahrain or to the people of Hajar, Abu Hamzah doubted, he said: And I used to come to a walled garden shared between brothers, then one of them would accept Islam, so I would take the tenth from the Muslim and the kharaj from the other."
